;; Reviewed 2026-10-09 (written by Claude, from the design, the MACRO
;; manual, LLVM's code generator and the debugger runs; for the user's
;; review). Why this is right:
;; - The main module of a program of two: poc -emit-macro32
;;   VaxExtension.mod writes it and its import's VaxExtLib.mar
;;   (expected-vax-VaxExtLib.mar), assembled and linked together.
;; - Phase 16 step 3 (section 14, item 11): a record's descriptor has its
;;   extension level, how many base types it has, after its size, and
;;   its base types' descriptors after the pointer count, the root first
;;   and its own last, BaseTypes[L] at 12 + 4 * L, as on LLVM. SquareDesc
;;   is level 1, VaxExtLib's ShapeDesc then its own; BigDesc level 2,
;;   ShapeDesc, CircleDesc, its own, then the offset of next, 8; Local's
;;   Ring, unnamed, L_TD_1, level 3, its inherited pointer at 8 too.
;;   Another module's descriptor is its symbol, declared .EXTERNAL.
;; - IS on a pointer: the pointer checked for NIL (trap 4 at the tested
;;   designator), its block's tag, -4(R0), into the same register, then
;;   the descriptor's level at least the type's, CMPL 4(R0), #L and BLSS
;;   (left out for a root), and BaseTypes[L] the type's descriptor, CMPL
;;   12+4*L(R0); R1 is set to 1 when both hold. On a VAR record parameter
;;   (Widen's d) the tag is the hidden one, 8(AP).
;; - A guard is the same test, trap 5 at the guarded designator when it
;;   fails; the variable is then used with the guard's type, so
;;   s(L.Circle).r := 6 dereferences s again (and checks it for NIL) and
;;   stores at 4(R0); t(Big).next(Square).side guards twice.
;; - WITH tests each guard in turn, and the first that holds runs its
;;   statements with the variable of the guard's type, then leaves; with
;;   none, the ELSE part (Kind's RETURN 1), or without one trap 6 at the
;;   WITH (Tag, line 40, column 5). Its NIL checks are at the WITH too.
;; - An assignment to a record whose dynamic type may differ from its
;;   static type, a VAR record parameter, guarded or not (Copy's d := e,
;;   Set's d(L.CircleDesc) := e), or p^ (t^ := sd): its tag, 8(AP) or
;;   -4(R0), compared with the static type's descriptor, else trap 13 at
;;   the statement (Oberon2.pdf 9.1), as on LLVM. A record assignment
;;   copies the target's size: sd := c^ the 4 bytes of a ShapeDesc.
;; - An inherited field is at its offset in the record that declares it:
;;   c.x at 0, c.y at 2, c.r at 4 (MemoryLayout wants the declaring
;;   record; VaxTypes.FieldOffset finds it).
;; - The run (run-values): tests 1101, area 75, kinds 2341, r 6, side 9,
;;   widened 10, tags 2740, sd 1 and 2, copied 12, assigned 809, local 3;
;;   b's and q's tags BigDesc's and SquareDesc's descriptors (their sizes
;;   12 and 6 shown), BigDesc's level 2, its base types ShapeDesc,
;;   CircleDesc and BigDesc. Modes 1 to 6 trap 5, 6, 13, 13, 13 and 4 at
;;   the positions above (run-*-trap).
; VaxExtension, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
